; Attribute copy chain (last 10 LDI), then the bitmap copy of the run begins
;
; The end of the chain of #R$9636, then the plain copy of the last attribute byte, then the set-up of the bitmap copy:
; the high byte of the attribute address is turned into the high byte of the screen address of the same cell row (the
; three thirds of the screen are $0800 apart), DE now addresses pixel row 0 of the last cell of the run, and HL the
; matching byte of the first pixel-row page of the redraw buffers (#R$C500 + index of the last cell). B = 4 pairs of
; pixel rows. C = $FF only keeps the LDD and LDI counting in BC from borrowing into B. It then falls into the JR at
; #R$9683, which enters the LDD chain of #R$9685; the loop of #R$96F3 comes back to the same JR for the next pair of
; pixel rows.
; .
; Hardware: writes the last attribute byte of the run and prepares screen addresses; the bitmap is written by the
; chains that follow.
;
; HL Redraw attribute buffer address of the last cell
; DE Attribute file address of the last cell
; O:HL Page $C5 address of the last cell
; O:DE Screen bitmap address of pixel row 0 of the last cell
; O:BC $04FF
@label=CopyAttrChain_Tail
c$9660 LDI           ;
 $9662 LDI           ;
 $9664 LDI           ;
 $9666 LDI           ;
 $9668 LDI           ;
 $966A LDI           ;
 $966C LDI           ;
 $966E LDI           ;
 $9670 LDI           ;
 $9672 LDI           ;
 $9674 LD A,(HL)     ; the last cell has no LDI
 $9675 LD (DE),A     ;
 $9676 LD A,D        ;
 $9677 ADD A,A       ;
 $9678 ADD A,A       ;
 $9679 ADD A,A       ;
@isub=AND THIRD_MASK
 $967A AND $18       ;
@isub=ADD A,SCREEN_HIGH
 $967C ADD A,$40     ;
 $967E LD D,A        ; D = high byte of the screen address
 $967F INC H         ; next page of the redraw buffer: pixel row 0
@isub=LD BC,PIXEL_ROW_PAIRS*256+$FF
 $9680 LD BC,$04FF   ; B = pairs of pixel rows, C = $FF so that LDD/LDI never borrow from B
; Self-modified: the offset byte of this JR is written by #R$9615 (2 x (32 - run length)). It enters the chain of LDD
; instructions at #R$9685 to copy one pixel row of the run from its last cell to its first; #R$96F3 jumps back here to
; do the next pair of pixel rows.
@label=SmcBitmapBackJump
*$9683 JR $9683      ; enter the LDD chain; the offset byte (+1) is patched
